From: Haiku Graviton <graviton@localhost>
Date: Mon, 25 Aug 2026 16:35:00 +0000
Subject: cmake/config.guess: recognise Haiku on arm64

The config.guess bundled with LLVM 12 is dated 2011-08-20 and knows only the
two Haiku hosts that existed then, BePC and x86_64. On arm64 "uname -m" reports
"arm64", so no case matches, the script prints its "unable to guess system
type" banner and exits non-zero. cmake/modules/GetHostTriple.cmake treats that
as fatal, so configure dies with "Failed to execute cmake/config.guess" before
a single object is compiled.

Add an arm64 case emitting the triple the toolchain itself reports, which is
aarch64-unknown-haiku as printed by "gcc [dash]dumpmachine", plus a generic
Haiku fallback so a future architecture degrades to a plausible guess rather
than aborting the configure outright.

diff --git a/cmake/config.guess b/cmake/config.guess
index 1315b1c8ba9c..2a3f4e5d6c71 100644
--- a/cmake/config.guess
+++ b/cmake/config.guess
@@ -1229,6 +1229,13 @@
     x86_64:Haiku:*:*) # Haiku running on x86_64.
 	echo x86_64-unknown-haiku
 	exit ;;
+    arm64:Haiku:*:*)	# Haiku on arm64. uname -m reports "arm64", but
+			# the toolchain triple is aarch64-unknown-haiku.
+	echo aarch64-unknown-haiku
+	exit ;;
+    *:Haiku:*:*)	# Any other Haiku architecture.
+	echo ${UNAME_MACHINE}-unknown-haiku
+	exit ;;
     SX-4:SUPER-UX:*:*)
 	echo sx4-nec-superux${UNAME_RELEASE}
 	exit ;;
